WEBVTT

00:00.050 --> 00:01.840
Every line on a graph

00:01.840 --> 00:03.875
does one of four things.

00:03.875 --> 00:05.991
It goes up, it goes down,

00:05.991 --> 00:07.130
it stays flat,

00:07.570 --> 00:08.700
or it zigzags.

00:09.040 --> 00:10.750
Let's find the right words for each one.

00:11.050 --> 00:12.975
When a line goes up, ask:

00:12.975 --> 00:14.752
how big was the change?

00:14.752 --> 00:18.010
A small rise: it rose slightly, or edged up.

00:18.690 --> 00:21.530
A moderate rise: it grew, or climbed.

00:22.170 --> 00:26.210
A big, fast rise: it surged, or it soared.

00:26.490 --> 00:28.397
Going down is the same.

00:28.397 --> 00:32.291
If it's small, then it dipped, or it eased back.

00:32.291 --> 00:35.390
If it's moderate, it fell, or declined.

00:35.550 --> 00:40.310
If it's large, then it plummeted, or collapsed.

00:40.590 --> 00:44.610
When the line stays flat, it remained stable,

00:44.610 --> 00:46.970
levelled off, or plateaued.

00:47.240 --> 00:48.765
And the zigzag.

00:48.765 --> 00:51.720
Here we say fluctuated, varied,

00:51.890 --> 00:54.880
was erratic, or rose and fell.

00:55.140 --> 00:58.573
Fluctuated isn't an increase or a decrease.

00:58.573 --> 01:01.070
It means repeated ups and downs.

01:01.330 --> 01:03.988
As an examiner, I often read paragraphs

01:03.988 --> 01:06.180
that use “increased” or “went up”

01:06.550 --> 01:07.530
five times.

01:07.530 --> 01:11.369
That will hold back your score for vocabulary,

01:11.369 --> 01:14.800
which is a quarter of your Task 1 mark. So

01:15.250 --> 01:16.770
first decide the direction,

01:17.310 --> 01:19.510
then decide how big the change was,

01:19.830 --> 01:22.533
and that's all you need to do at first.

01:22.533 --> 01:24.897
Now, try the activity on the right

01:24.897 --> 01:27.600
and sort each verb into the right group.
